This is a classic and very common data discrepancy bug. The root cause lies in how Spring Data JPA automatically generates SQL queries from long method names.
Here is exactly why this happened:
 1. **The Branch Bug:** Your BranchMasterRepository was completely missing the Status check in its method signature, meaning it searched the entire database including closed/inactive branches.
 2. **The CGL Bug:** Your CglMasterRepository *did* have the status check (...AndStatusEquals), but in Spring Data JPA, OR has lower precedence than AND. This means the database read the query as: *"Find CGLs where the Description matches AND Status is Active, **OR** where just the CGL Number matches (ignoring status completely)."*
Because the Bulk Upload uses ValidationMasterService (which has strict SQL queries), it correctly rejected them, while the UI repositories allowed them through.
To fix this permanently without breaking your services, we need to override the Spring JPA auto-generation by providing an explicit @Query with strict parentheses.
Here are the exact replacements for both files.
### 1. Fix the Branch Repository
**File:** BranchMasterRepository.java
Replace the **entire file** with this to add the explicit status = 1 check:
```java
package com.fincore.VoucherService.Repository;

import org.springframework.data.domain.Pageable;
import org.springframework.data.jpa.repository.JpaRepository;
import org.springframework.data.jpa.repository.Query;
import org.springframework.data.repository.query.Param;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Repository;

import com.fincore.VoucherService.Models.BranchMaster;

import java.util.List;

@Repository
public interface BranchMasterRepository extends JpaRepository<BranchMaster, String> {

    // FIX: Added explicit @Query to enforce STATUS = 1 (Active) for all manual searches
    @Query("SELECT b FROM BranchMaster b WHERE b.status = 1 AND (LOWER(b.name) LIKE LOWER(CONCAT('%', :name, '%')) OR LOWER(b.code) LIKE LOWER(CONCAT('%', :code, '%')))")
    List<BranchMaster> findByNameContainingIgnoreCaseOrCodeContainingIgnoreCase(@Param("name") String name, @Param("code") String code, Pageable pageable);
}

```
### 2. Fix the CGL Repository
**File:** CglMasterRepository.java
Replace the **entire file** with this to fix the OR logic precedence:
```java
package com.fincore.VoucherService.Repository;

import org.springframework.data.domain.Pageable;
import org.springframework.data.jpa.repository.JpaRepository;
import org.springframework.data.jpa.repository.Query;
import org.springframework.data.repository.query.Param;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Repository;

import com.fincore.VoucherService.Models.CglMaster;

import java.util.List;

@Repository
public interface CglMasterRepository extends JpaRepository<CglMaster, String> {

    // FIX: Added explicit @Query with parentheses. This forces BOTH CGL Number and Description searches to respect the STATUS flag.
    @Query("SELECT c FROM CglMaster c WHERE c.status = :status AND (LOWER(c.cglNumber) LIKE LOWER(CONCAT('%', :cglNumber, '%')) OR LOWER(c.description) LIKE LOWER(CONCAT('%', :description, '%')))")
    List<CglMaster> findByCglNumberContainingIgnoreCaseOrDescriptionContainingIgnoreCaseAndStatusEquals(
            @Param("cglNumber") String cglNumber, 
            @Param("description") String description, 
            @Param("status") Integer status, 
            Pageable pageable
    );
}

```
### Why this fixes the issue:
By adding the @Query annotation, we lock down the SQL logic. The frontend UI drop-downs will now execute these strict queries and completely filter out any inactive Branches and CGLs.
*(Note: Your CurrencyController already calls validationMasterService.getAllActiveCurrencies(), so it is already perfectly aligned with the Bulk Upload logic. Fixing the Branch and CGL repositories completely synchronizes your manual and bulk validation rules.)*
